# "This creature becomes a copy of another target creature you control": Silent Hallcreeper (1/1) takes the counters on turn 3 (3/3), then on turn 5
# becomes a copy of Bot1's Ornithopter, a 0/2 flying artifact creature (CR 707.2): it keeps its two +1/+1 counters (so it is 2/4), loses its Horror
# subtype and its own abilities, and the Ornithopter is untouched. Ornithopter is its only legal target (it is "another" creature), so it is chosen without asking.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Silent Hallcreeper
Ornithopter
Island x21

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x24

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Silent Hallcreeper.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Silent Hallcreeper > Bot2)
Bot1.Modes(Put two)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Silent Hallcreeper > Bot2)
Bot1.Modes(This creature becomes a copy)

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot1.Battlefield = Ornithopter; Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Keywords = Flying
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.ChosenModes = 1, 3
